      "english": "In the specification of Proposition II.13, the nominative phrase τὸ ἀπὸ τῆς ΑΓ τετράγωνον serves as the subject being compared, while the genitive τῶν ἀπὸ τῶν ΓΒ, ΒΑ τετραγώνων acts as the genitive of comparison for \"than\". Furthermore, the dative phrase τῷ δὶς ὑπὸ τῶν ΓΒ, ΒΔ περιεχομένῳ ὀρθογωνίῳ expresses the degree of difference \"by how much\" the square is less.",
