      "english": "As David Wihl explained in our Group 4 presentation, the enunciation of Proposition II.12 for obtuse-angled triangles, ἀμβλυγωνίοις τριγώνοις, differs from II.13 by exactly seven corresponding word pairs. For instance, II.12 states that the square is greater, μεῖζόν ἐστι, and that the perpendicular falls outside, ἐκτός, whereas II.13 states it is less, ἔλαττόν ἐστι, and that the perpendicular falls inside, ἐντός.",
